# demo-runner

## A typewriter-style scripted terminal demo player.
## Headings with one hash appear instantly, descriptions with two.

This plain line is narrative text — printed verbatim.

$ echo "This command was typed character-by-character, then executed."

# Directives

## @sleep pauses, @input simulates the operator typing,
## and @clear wipes the screen.

@sleep 1

@input simulated keystrokes appear like this

$ printf 'Side effects are real: anything a shell can do.\n'

$ echo "Each command pauses briefly so viewers can follow along."

@clear

# Speed Control

## Re-run with --fast, --slow, --speed medium, or --no-pause.
## Or export DEMO_RUNNER_SPEED=fast (TABBING_DEMO_SPEED also works).

$ echo "Try: demo-runner --fast examples/tour.demo"

# Going Further

## examples/tabbing-on-tour.demo drives terminal tab titles via the
## optional tabbing-on integration — it needs tabbing-on installed.

$ echo "Enjoy!"
